ANACREON 12
"Arronax"
0	; Random Scenario
1 4	; One to four players
45	; 45 x 45 grid
200   ; 200 planets
1     ; Intermediate
100 0 ; 100 + years
7054	; starting year

; This scenario was created by Adam Luker
; (zot@aapc.com), in the hopes that it might 
; be enjoyed.

BEGINTEXT
                              

                              ***** Arronax *****

               Just after the collapse of the second great empire,  
       mankind lived in a divided but still intact society.  Lacking
       the catastrophic disarray of the first fall, many worlds remained
       self-sufficient and conservative.  Any world that seemed to step
       out of line was swiftly punished by its neighbors.  But human 
       nature soon required men once again to look to the stars and 
       dream of expansion.  Some worlds set up huge industries devoted 
       to shipbuilding so they could again roam the galaxy."  

NEWPAGE                
                              
                              ***** Arronax *****   

               "However, one province had somehow escaped the tide of 
       the fall and was able to keep its integrity.  It grew accustomed
       to supremacy and extremely discouraged others from attempting 
       to become powerful.  Arronax, a divided kingdom, was ruled by rival
       twin magistrates which sometimes clashed, but they were both violent-
       ly opposed to others "poaching" in their territory, which they felt 
       to be the entire galaxy."  
                                        
                                        - History of the Galaxy
                                          Zex Narphil, Counselor
        
NEWPAGE
                              
                              ***** Arronax *****    

               You are controlling an empire that is desperate for 
       expansion.  Your two planets are overflowing with ships and 
       pilgrims who want to try their luck at a new frontier.  They
       grow increasingly restless and your throne is in danger.  You 
       must overthrow the Arronaxan empires and once again establish 
       harmony in the galaxy.

               You must be cautious.  Not all emperors have such noble 
       motives as do you.  Many are once again learning the skills of 
       piracy, and of building conquering machines; colossal structures
       which fill an entire sector.  Your mission will not be easy, but
       you must succeed in order to advance.  Already your planet is being
       probed by Arronax...

NEWPAGE

ENDTEXT

; --- World flavor text ---

BEGINDESCRIPTION

WorldBackgroundIndex
2:1 E:0          1 ; Player 1 Capital
2:3 E:1          1 ; Player 2 Capital
2:5 E:2          1 ; Player 3 Capital
2:6 E:3          1 ; Player 4 Capital
2:8 E:4          2 ; Arronax 1 (empire 5)
2:12 E:5         2 ; Arronax 2 (empire 6)
2:16 E:6         3 ; Empire 7, the pirates
2:17 E:7         4 ; Empire 8, the berzerker empire
3:1 E:7          5 ; Rogue Starbase
EndIndex

TEXT 1
Only by defeating Arronax will you be able to expand your empire.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 2
One of the Arronaxan capitals, this is one of your primary targets
ENDTEXT

TEXT 3
This is the capital of the pirate empire.  An effecient 
jumpbase, it would be a strong asset under your flag.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 4
This world controls the Starbase that roams these sectors. 
Conquering this planet would most effectively stop the 
starbase from tormenting you.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 5
This starbase poses a great threat to your systems.  By 
disabling the planet that controls it, you can stop it
from ravaging your worlds.  That won't be so easy, though.
ENDTEXT

ENDDESCRIPTION

